# 803 historical-only selected metadata (inert)

New historical_metadata is a fixed internal consumer of an already registered selected worklist. It pins exact configuration ID/case/D11 component and selected kind/record/case/scope/owner_policy before permission computation, and compares the same map after. Retraction also pins claim_id. Only scalar values lists are used; note, actor, source body, claim_ids and selected_claim are not hydrated. Null/wrong policy and incomplete request sets fail closed, rather than being silently projected.

The private scope-only pipeline freshly revalidates inventory, composes all Finance then PMO permissions, consumes its authentic receipt, computes scope restrictions, and repeats inventory/scope checks. It never calls source eligibility/public_evidence. The existing full facts API retains combined scope and source semantics through shared _compute_scopes and _compute_sources. Scope and full receipts have distinct exact types/registries, cannot cross purposes, and are one-use; old/current misuse poisons both. Both retain bounded counters and original native reader predicates.

Historical workbench rows are gated by visible_scopes. Its source choices/body history independently use visible_sources. Accordingly the metadata consumer denies only if a selected record's own scope is hidden: it does not require every linked scope visible or own/ancestor evidence eligible. Finance empty-scope restriction and all historical claims remain in shared scope computation. This is NOT permission to expose source text. Broader scalar dependency discovery remains an engineering admission limit, not an assertion of the native workbench's complete allowed set.

Output is only id/kind/metadata_only/domain_route/owner_policy/historical-state/effects_performed; retraction additionally records historical_retraction_recorded. No owner_current call or false stand-in, no status/selection/latest-resolution inference. Retractions remain history. Existing original actor owner-current predicates and prepared resolver integration remain unresolved and unclaimed.

Caller duties remain the authenticated outer snapshot entry and actual policy-impact configuration/origin gates. No registry, adapter migration, route, capture/review/agent adoption or production wiring is installed. The fixed trusted read-only sequence has no caller callbacks, but is not a defense against arbitrary same-connection mutation after return. Selected mapping comparison is not through-commit authorization. Full source API retains its explicitly unbounded native forecast predicate inner DB work; scope-only API does not invoke it.

Fourteen new fake-transport pure tests cover scope/full separation, exact scalar maps and retraction relationship mutation, closed output/no deferred fields, independent source versus selected-scope restrictions, wrong case/config/strict IDs and old/current poison. Combined prior tests are retained. No SQL/native fixtures were executed; native equivalence, actual query plans/concurrency and lifecycle/route integration remain UNRUN. Backup snapshot95afd305 remains unchanged and does not cover this later candidate automatically.
